            "title": "National Mineral Policy (NMP 2019): Private Participation, Dedicated Corridors & Inter-Generational Equity",
            "summary": "",
            "theoryHtml": "\n            <h3>National Mineral Policy (NMP 2019): Strategic Objectives & Paradigm Shifts</h3>\n            <p>Approved by the Union Cabinet in February 2019, the <strong>National Mineral Policy 2019 (NMP 2019)</strong> replaced the earlier National Mineral Policy 2008. Formulated on the recommendations of the high-level committee chaired by <strong>Dr. K.R. Rao</strong>, it introduced a modern, transparent, and environmentally sustainable framework for non-coal and non-fuel minerals.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. Core Strategic Objectives of NMP 2019</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Expansion of Domestic Mineral Output:</strong> Aims to <strong>increase domestic mineral production by 200%</strong> in 7 years, significantly reducing India’s burgeoning trade deficit in industrial minerals and metals.</li>\n                <li><strong>Enhanced Private Sector Role:</strong> Encourages the private sector to take up exploration of deep-seated and concealed deposits by granting rights over reconnaissance and prospecting data and creating an open-door regulatory climate.</li>\n                <li><strong>Dedicated Mineral Corridors:</strong> Proposes dedicated logistics corridors—integrating railway freight lines, inland waterways, and coastal shipping—to streamline mineral evacuation from remote mining belts to smelting plants and export harbors.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>2. The Concept of Inter-Generational Equity & Sovereign Mineral Funds</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Inter-Generational Equity:</strong> Minerals are finite, non-renewable geological resources. NMP 2019 explicitly enshrines the principle of inter-generational equity—treating mineral wealth as a <em>shared national inheritance</em> across present and future generations.</li>\n                <li><strong>State Mineral Development Funds:</strong> Encourages states to benchmark mineral depletion against long-term investments in alternative human and financial capital, supporting the creation of local sovereign wealth funds or future-generation trust accounts (e.g., following the Goa Iron Ore Supreme Court ruling and the Norwegian Sovereign Wealth Fund model).</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>3. Modernizing Exploration, Technology & Environmental Sustainability</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Right of First Refusal:</strong> Provides a right of first refusal at the time of auction to holders of reconnaissance permits or prospecting licenses, encouraging private risk-capital in high-risk baseline mineral prospecting.</li>\n                <li><strong>Coastal and Offshore Mining:</strong> Emphasizes exploration and sustainable exploitation of minerals from coastal beach placers and offshore exclusive economic zones (EEZ).</li>\n                <li><strong>Star Rating of Mines:</strong> Mandatory adoption of a sustainable development framework where operating mines are evaluated and accorded <em>Star Ratings</em> (1 to 5 stars) based on environmental management, digital monitoring, community rehabilitation, and mine safety.</li>\n                <li><strong>Merger and Acquisition Facilitation:</strong> Promotes consolidation and rationalization of small, unviable mineral leases into larger, mechanized mining blocks to achieve economies of scale.</li>\n            </ul>\n        ",
            "pointsToRemember": [
                "NMP 2019 was formulated based on the recommendations of the Dr. K.R. Rao Committee, replacing NMP 2008.",
                "Aimed to increase domestic mineral production by 200% in 7 years to reduce the mineral trade deficit.",
                "Introduced the concept of dedicated mineral logistics corridors (rail, waterways, coastal shipping).",
                "Explicitly recognized Inter-Generational Equity, treating minerals as a shared inheritance for future generations.",
                "Established the Star Rating system (1 to 5 stars) for evaluating sustainable development in operating mines.",
                "Supported the creation of State Mineral Development Funds to safeguard wealth for future generations."
            ],
            "keyNotes": [
                "NMP 2019 pivoted India's mining strategy toward private risk exploration, dedicated mineral evacuation corridors, and the constitutional doctrine of inter-generational equity."
            ],
