            "summary": "",
            "theoryHtml": "\n            <h3>Khanij Bidesh India Limited (KABIL): Overseas Strategic Resource Acquisition</h3>\n            <p>To ensure national raw material sovereignty for the electric vehicle revolution, semiconductor manufacturing, and renewable power infrastructure, India must secure access to critical minerals that are scarce within its domestic borders. In August 2019, the Ministry of Mines established <strong>Khanij Bidesh India Limited (KABIL)</strong> to identify and acquire critical mineral assets overseas.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. Corporate Structure & Equity Shareholding</h4>\n            <p>KABIL is a dedicated joint venture company constituted by three premier Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs) under the Ministry of Mines:</p>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>National Aluminium Company Limited (NALCO):</strong> Holds a <strong>40% equity share</strong> (lead partner).</li>\n                <li><strong>Hindustan Copper Limited (HCL):</strong> Holds a <strong>30% equity share</strong>.</li>\n                <li><strong>Mineral Exploration and Consultancy Limited (MECL):</strong> Holds a <strong>30% equity share</strong>.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>2. Core Mandate & Target Mineral Suite</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Mandate:</strong> Identify, explore, acquire, develop, mine, process, and commercially procure strategic and critical minerals overseas for supply to the Indian market.</li>\n                <li><strong>Strategic Focus Minerals:</strong> <strong>Lithium (Li), Cobalt (Co), Nickel (Ni), and Rare Earth Elements (REEs)</strong>.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>3. Landmark Breakthrough: Argentina's Lithium Triangle (January 2024)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>The Lithium Triangle:</strong> The world's richest lithium brine basin, spanning the high-altitude Andean salt flats (Salars) across <strong>Argentina, Bolivia, and Chile</strong>, containing over 50% of the world's known lithium resources.</li>\n                <li><strong>The Historic Catamarca Agreement:</strong> In January 2024, KABIL signed a milestone exploration and development agreement with <strong>CAMYEN</strong> (Catamarca Minera y Energética Sociedad del Estado), the state-owned mining enterprise of Catamarca Province, Argentina.</li>\n                <li><strong>Scope of Acquisition:</strong>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li>Acquisition of <strong>five lithium brine blocks</strong>: <em>Cortadera-I, Cortadera-VII, Cortadera-VIII, Cateo-2022-018, and Cortadera-VI</em>, covering an extensive area of approximately 15,703 hectares.</li>\n                        <li>Total project investment commitment of over <strong>₹200 crore</strong>.</li>\n                        <li>Grants KABIL exclusive exploration and commercial exploitation rights to pump brine, concentrate lithium carbonate, and export refined battery-grade lithium directly to India.</li>\n                        <li>Marks <strong>India's first-ever overseas critical mineral exploration and commercial mining venture</strong> by a public sector enterprise.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>4. Engagements in Australia & Chile</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Australia:</strong> KABIL partnered with the Critical Minerals Facilitation Office (CMFO) of Australia under the <em>Critical Minerals Investment Partnership</em>, conducting joint due diligence on lithium and cobalt greenfield and brownfield projects in Western Australia.</li>\n                <li><strong>Chile:</strong> Initiated government-to-government negotiations with state-owned enterprises (CODELCO and ENAMI) to explore joint ventures in Chilean copper and lithium brine salars.</li>\n            </ul>\n        ",
